            <div xml:id="d431">

                <pb facs="0494" n="376" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg376"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.113/10500: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Ciudad Juarez</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dye</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">El
                                Paso, Tex</hi></placeName>., <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-01">April 1, 1929</date>.<lb/>[Received 7:23
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Rebels in Juarez claim to have there nine airplanes. Believe this is exaggerated.
                    Am reliably informed they bought three planes in <pb facs="0495" n="377"
                        xml:id="pg377"/> Phoenix, paying $7,000 apiece, and one trimotor in Los
                    Angeles. These planes crossed to Mexico from El Paso Friday and Saturday nights
                    with American pilots. Rebels seem to have plenty of money and is open secret
                    that much ammunition and materials crossing to Mexico.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dye</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
